      "bbox": [
        185,
        897,
        1497,
        1162
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "d. A covered business or vendor on a street where a covered business is using an outdoor commercial premises must allow for a minimum eight (8) foot clearance for pedestrian traffic on the sidewalk at all times. Obstructions such as parking meters, traffic signs, tree pits that are flush with sidewalk grade, and street lamp posts shall not detract from the measurement of the eight foot clearance; however the calculation of the minimum eight (8) foot clearance shall be unencumbered of any street furniture including permanent benches, bicycle parking, tree pits with guard rails, and kiosks.",
